on window with 10-min gap, count elements per window\n3. This gives us (jobId, sessionCount) for each session\n4. Then key by jobId again and take the max\n5. Read job events, filter FINISH, get set of finished jobIds\n6. Join/filter the results to only include finished jobs\n\nBut the join is the tricky part in streaming. Since this is essentially a batch job (finite data), I can use DataStream with bounded sources and it will work.\n\nLet me use a cleaner approach: process all task submit events with session windows to get per-session counts, then use a process function to find the max per job, then join with finished jobs.\n\nFor the join with finished jobs, I can use a `connect` + `CoProcessFunction` or I can simply collect all finished jobs to a set and use a `RichFilterFunction` with broadcast state. But that adds complexity.\n\nA simpler approach: use `KeyedCoProcessFunction` - connect the max-session-per-job stream with the finished-jobs stream, keyed by jobId. When both have been seen, emit the result.\n\nActually, since this is bounded data, the simplest approach would be to:\n1. Process task SUBMIT events in session windows → (jobId, count) per session\n2. Then keyBy(jobId) and reduce to max → (jobId, maxCount)\n3. Read job FINISH events → set of finished jobIds  \n4. Connect these two streams and output when we have both\n\nLet me implement this."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":259,"cache_read_input_tokens":69474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":259,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtBGT5HVeR9CwnErQZJ6","type":"assistant","uuid":"df1da542-efe9-40f9-8b77-61bf38f99540","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:44:59.675Z"}
